While playing in this year's tournament, I realized I simply didn't
have the time or patience to bang out an extinctionist.  There are so
many quality hackers in the tourney, my simple ascensions don't have a
chance!

So, I thought: what if monsters, upon reaching the usual extinction
threshold, began to evolve and become more powerful?  I've written a
patch to do just that which should apply cleanly against v3.4.3
vanilla:

http://slackmaster.net/~burt/nethack/evolution-v0.2.patch

Upon reaching MAXMONNO (set to 120 currently), the amount of damage
dealt per hit for a given species will increase continuously and
exponentially:

# born      Damage Multiplier
120           1.0
240           4.0
360           8.0
480          16.0

Species that become extinct earlier (Nazguls and Erinyes) follow the
previous extinction rules.  There is a scaling factor that can be
changed to adjust the game balance as well. I believe this breaks both
bonesfile and savefile compatibility since I had to enlarge a few data
structures.

I don't usually write for code as flexible as the nethack sources, so I
had a few questions:

1. I referenced MAX_INT from limits.h -- should this be hardcoded
instead?
2. I needed to enlarge all of the members of the mvitals struct, but as
with the rest of the code I wrote it is wrapped in an #ifdef.  Should I
have enlarged it for both cases (otherwise, savefile/bonefile
compatibility will break depending on if it compiled in or out?)

